55885	55990	55882	55883	Dick Flairer	509	" I was up Hackney way , expecting to do a little business with Tom the Cracksman,[26 ] which did n't come off ; for Tom had been at the boozing - ken[27 ] all the night before , and had blowed his hand up in a lark with some davy's - dust.[28 ] Well , I wus coming home again , infernal sulky at the affair 's breaking down , when just as I got to Cambridge - Heath - gate I heerd the gallopin ' of horses . I looks round , nat'rally enough;--but who should I see upon a lovely chestnut mare---- "
