438414	438546	438555	438555	Isabella	495	" Oh ! if ever this fond aspiration should be realised,--if ever the humble and obscure Englishman were united to the high - born and brilliant Italian Princess , how sweet -- how sweet would it be for him to owe rank and fortune to the woman whom he loved so fondly , and whom he would ever love until the hand of Death should beckon him to the tomb ! For myself , I pant not for the honours and glories of this life ; for hadst thou , Isabella , been the daughter of the lowest peasants , I had loved thee all the same -- and had been far , far more contented , because the obstacles which now oppose our happiness might then have ceased to exist ! "
