513455	513606	513608	513609	the king	14889	" Most loyal and dutiful friends , this is the hundred and thirty - first anniversary of the institution of that custom in virtue of which the provincial rulers of the united races of Egyptians and Bohemians in England assemble together once every year at the Palace . A hundred and thirty - one years ago , this house was purchased by my grandfather King Sisman , and bequeathed to his descendants to serve as the head - quarters and central point of our administration . There is scarcely an individual of the united races who has not experienced the hospitality of this Palace . Every worthy Zingaree who visits the metropolis enjoys his bed and his board without fee and without price for seven days in our mansion , the superintendence of which is so ably conducted , while we are absent , by our brother on my right . "
